 You're absolutely right! The Rich Text Editor can be quite limiting. Let's replace it with a simple multiline text input.

## Replace the Rich Text Editor

**Remove**: `rtAEContent` (Rich Text Editor)

**Add**: Text Input control with these properties:

**Text Input Properties:**
- **Name**: `txtAEContent`
- **Mode**: `TextMode.MultiLine`
- **X**: `20`
- **Y**: `207`
- **Width**: `1294`
- **Height**: `170`
- **BorderColor**: `RGBA(245, 245, 245, 1)`
- **Font**: `Font.'Segoe UI'`
- **Size**: `14`
- **HintText**: `"Enter update content here..."`
- **PaddingTop**: `10`
- **PaddingLeft**: `10`
- **PaddingRight**: `10`
- **PaddingBottom**: `10`

## Update Your Save Button Formula

Change the OnSelect formula for `btnAESave` to use the new text input:

```
If(
    And(
        !IsBlank(txtAETitle.Text),
        ddAEHotels.Selected.Value <> "---All Hotels---",
        !IsBlank(ddAEUpdateType.Selected.Value),
        !IsBlank(dpAEUpdateDate.SelectedDate),
        !IsBlank(txtAEContent.Text)
    ),
    Patch(
        HotelUpdates,
        Defaults(HotelUpdates),
        {
            Title: txtAETitle.Text,
            Hotel: ddAEHotels.Selected.Value,
            UpdateType: ddAEUpdateType.Selected.Value,
            UpdateDate: dpAEUpdateDate.SelectedDate,
            Content: txtAEContent.Text,
            Image: If(IsBlank(btnAEAddImage.Media), Blank(), btnAEAddImage.Media)
        }
    );
    Notify("Entry saved successfully!", NotificationType.Success);
    Reset(txtAETitle);
    Reset(ddAEHotels);
    Reset(ddAEUpdateType);
    Reset(dpAEUpdateDate);
    Reset(txtAEContent);
    Reset(btnAEAddImage);
    Set(showAddEntry, false);
    Set(showAdminGallery, true),
    Notify("Please fill in all required fields (marked with *)", NotificationType.Error)
)
```

## Update Cancel Button

Also update the Cancel button to reset the new text input:

```
Reset(txtAETitle);
Reset(ddAEHotels);
Reset(ddAEUpdateType);
Reset(dpAEUpdateDate);
Reset(txtAEContent);
Reset(btnAEAddImage);
Set(showAddEntry, false);
Set(showAdminGallery, true)
```

This gives you a clean, simple multiline text box that's much more reliable than the Rich Text Editor!

